#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Controls"
msgstr "SeHmey"

# review: "nach De'wI'" (head computer) coined for headset
#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"One client runs on a desktop, a phone and a headset, so every action has a "
"way in from each of them. The keyboard has the most; touch, a gamepad and "
"the XR controllers carry the actions a match needs, and the Settings menu "
"reaches the rest -- including from a headset, where there is no keyboard at "
"all. This page is also the in-game help's (`/` or `?`)."
msgstr ""
"raSDaq De'wI', ghogh HablI', nach De'wI' je lo' wa' ghun, vaj Hoch vangvaD "
"He ghaj Hoch De'wI'. law'qu' leQ'echlet; Quj vangmey poQlu'bogh luqeng Hot, "
"Quj SeHwI', XR SeHwI'mey je, 'ej latlh SIch SeHlaw HIDjolev -- nach "
"De'wI'vo' je, pa' leQ'echlet tu'lu'be'. Quj QaH (`/` pagh `?`) 'oH je "
"ghItlhvam'e'."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Keyboard"
msgstr "leQ'echlet"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Driving"
msgstr "Duj chIj"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`W` / `S` or `Up` / `Down` — move forward/backward"
msgstr "`W` / `S` pagh `Up` / `Down` — yIghoS/yIDoH"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`A` / `D` or `Left` / `Right` — turn left/right"
msgstr "`A` / `D` pagh `Left` / `Right` — poS/nIH yItlhe'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Enter` — shoot"
msgstr "`Enter` — yIbach"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Tab` — jump"
msgstr "`Tab` — yISup"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Space` — drop flag"
msgstr "`Space` — joqwI' yIchagh"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`I` or right-click — identify the tank in your sights, and lock a Guided "
"Missile onto it"
msgstr ""
"`I` pagh nIH chu' — Duj DaDoSbogh yIngu', 'ej ghaHvaD peng SeHlu'bogh "
"yIDoSmoH"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Delete` — self-destruct, after a five second countdown; `Delete` again "
"calls it off"
msgstr ""
"`Delete` — vagh lup pIq yIQaw''egh; `Delete` Dayuvqa'DI' qIllu'"

# review: "corner" rendered as "tlhoy'mey ngeD" (between walls)
#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`9` or `/autopilot [roger|ace]` — autopilot: the pilot drives, aims and "
"shoots until pressed again. `Settings -> Autopilot` chooses the pilot "
"without a keyboard. You can still drive while it does, to help it out of a "
"corner -- see [Combining inputs](#combining-inputs)"
msgstr ""
"`9` pagh `/autopilot [roger|ace]` — nIteb chIjwI': chIj, DoS, bach je "
"chIjwI', Dayuvqa'pa'. leQ'echlet Hutlhbogh chIjwI' wIv `Settings -> "
"Autopilot`. chIjtaHvIS ghaH bIchIjlaH je, tlhoy'mey ngeDvo' ghaH DaQaHmeH "
"-- yIlegh [SeHmey muv](#combining-inputs)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`P` — pause/resume"
msgstr "`P` — yImev/yItaghqa'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Chat"
msgstr "ja'chuq"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`N` — open chat (or click the `Send` button)"
msgstr "`N` — ja'chuq yIpoSmoH (pagh `Send` leQ yIchu')"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Enter` — send chat (while chat input is focused, or click `Send` again)"
msgstr ""
"`Enter` — ja'chuq yIngeH (ja'chuq ghItlhwI' DaSeHtaHvIS, pagh `Send` "
"yIchu'qa')"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`1` / `2` / `3` / `4` / `5` — switch chat tab (`All` / `Chat` / `Server` / "
"`Misc` / `Debug`)"
msgstr ""
"`1` / `2` / `3` / `4` / `5` — ja'chuq pa' yIchoH (`All` / `Chat` / `Server` "
"/ `Misc` / `Debug`)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`[` / `]` — previous/next chat tab"
msgstr "`[` / `]` — ja'chuq pa' nubwI'/veb"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Tab` — while typing, complete a player, command or flag name; `@` starts a "
"mention and `#` a player's slot number"
msgstr ""
"`Tab` — bIghItlhtaHvIS, QujwI' pong, ra' pong, joqwI' pong ghap yIrInmoH; "
"pong tagh `@`, 'ej QujwI' Daq mI' tagh `#`"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Up` / `Down` — while typing, recall earlier lines; type the start of a line "
"first to recall only the ones beginning that way"
msgstr ""
"`Up` / `Down` — bIghItlhtaHvIS, tlheghmey ngo' yIqaw; tlhegh bI'reS "
"yIghItlh wa'DIch, vaj tlheghmey taghbogh mIwvetlh neH Daqaw"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`.` — reply to last direct-message sender"
msgstr "`.` — SoHvaD QIn ngeHwI' Qav yIjang"

# review: "nemesis" rendered as "jagh'a'lIj" (your great enemy)
#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`,` — message nemesis target"
msgstr "`,` — jagh'a'lIjvaD QIn yIngeH"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Page Up` / `Page Down` — scroll chat history"
msgstr "`Page Up` / `Page Down` — ja'chuq qun yIvIH"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`End` — jump chat to newest message"
msgstr "`End` — QIn chu'qu' yISIch"

# review: no Klingon word for "copy"; "yIlIngqa'" (produce again) coined
#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Drag across the history while chat is open to select it, then copy; typing "
"carries on in the input"
msgstr ""
"ja'chuq poSmoHlu'taHvIS, qun yIlIS 'ej yIwIv, vaj yIlIngqa'; ghItlhwI'Daq "
"ghItlh ghoStaH ghItlh"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "View and panels"
msgstr "legh 'ej 'echletmey"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Esc` — back out one step: exit chat input, leave fullscreen, leave mouse "
"steering, then open Settings. Pressing it again closes Settings, so it is "
"always safe to press one more time"
msgstr ""
"`Esc` — wa' mIw yIDoH: ja'chuq ghItlhwI' yImej, Hoch HaSta yImej, mouse chIj "
"yImej, vaj SeHlaw yIpoSmoH. Dayuvqa'chugh SeHlaw SoQmoH, vaj reH Qob'be' "
"latlh yuvlu'chugh"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`M` — toggle mouse steering"
msgstr "`M` — mouse chIj yIchu'/yIchu'Ha'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`C` — cycle camera mode"
msgstr "`C` — mIllogh qonwI' lo' yIchoH"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`O` — toggle operator panel"
msgstr "`O` — vu'wI' 'echlet yI'agh/yISo'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`F` — toggle fullscreen"
msgstr "`F` — Hoch HaSta yIchu'/yIchu'Ha'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`` ` `` — toggle debug HUD"
msgstr "`` ` `` — Qagh HUD yI'agh/yISo'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`=` or `+` or `Numpad +` — zoom radar out (increase range)"
msgstr "`=` pagh `+` pagh `Numpad +` — noch chuq yIDuy'moH (chuq yIghurmoH)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`-` or `Numpad -` — zoom radar in (decrease range)"
msgstr "`-` pagh `Numpad -` — noch chuq yIlaghmoH (chuq yI'ovmoH)"

# review: "zoom" verbs coined; check against the interface's radar strings
#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`\\` — reset radar zoom to the default medium range (half the world's radar "
"limit, which is the world size unless the map says otherwise)"
msgstr ""
"`\\` — noch chuq motlh yIchegh: chuq bID (qo' noch veH bID; qo' Hugh 'oH, "
"latlh ja'be'chugh pu'jIn)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Settings -> Radar: ...` — cycle Short/Medium/Long radar presets"
msgstr "`Settings -> Radar: ...` — noch chuq motlh yIchoH: ngaj/bID/nI'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`B` — toggle the voice microphone"
msgstr "`B` — ghogh jan yIchu'/yIchu'Ha'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Settings -> Audio Settings` — set the game, voice, and microphone levels, "
"and choose the voice channel: All, Nearby, or Team"
msgstr ""
"`Settings -> Audio Settings` — Quj, ghogh, ghogh jan je HoS yIlan, 'ej ghogh "
"He yIwIv: Hoch, Sumbogh, boq ghap"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`/` or `?` — show/hide help panel"
msgstr "`/` pagh `?` — QaH 'echlet yI'agh/yISo'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`🎤` beside the gear — the microphone, as `B` is: a green border means you "
"are transmitting and a red one means you are not, and the hover text names "
"the channel it would speak on"
msgstr ""
"`🎤` SeHlaw retlhDaq — ghogh jan 'oH, `B` rur: SuDbogh HeH ngeHtaH SoH 'e' "
"maq, Doqbogh HeH ngeHbe' SoH 'e' maq, 'ej ghogh He ponglu'bogh cha' "
"ghItlh, Dung ghoS cursor'e'"

# review: long sentence restructured; "chevron"-free, but check the borrowing logic reads
#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`▲` beside the gear — hide the scoreboard and chat, leaving the name row and "
"the chat tabs; `▼` brings them back. Typing a message borrows the chat "
"window until you are done with it, and `U` or `7` borrows the scoreboard "
"until the hunt cursor closes; tapping a chat tab opens chat for good. Small "
"screens start collapsed"
msgstr ""
"`▲` SeHlaw retlhDaq — mI' 'echlet ja'chuq je yISo'; pong tlhegh ja'chuq "
"pa'mey je ratlh. chaq lucheghmoH `▼`. QIn DaghItlhtaHvIS ja'chuq Qorwagh "
"Dalo' bIrInpa', 'ej wam cursor SoQpa' mI' 'echlet lo' `U` pagh `7`; ja'chuq "
"pa' DaHotchugh reH poSmoHlu' ja'chuq. HaSta mach So'lu'taH tagh"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Settings -> Anaglyph 3D` — red/cyan glasses; `Settings -> VR Mode` enters a "
"WebXR headset"
msgstr ""
"`Settings -> Anaglyph 3D` — Doq/SuDqu' mIn botlhmey; `Settings -> VR Mode` "
"WebXR nach De'wI' 'el"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Menus"
msgstr "HIDjolevmey"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Up` / `Down` — previous/next control, including from inside a text field"
msgstr ""
"`Up` / `Down` — SeHwI' nubwI'/veb, ghItlh yotlh qoDvo' je"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Left` / `Right` — change the focused control: move a slider, pick the next "
"choice. In a text field they move the cursor instead"
msgstr ""
"`Left` / `Right` — SeHwI' DaSeHbogh yIchoH: SIqwI' yIvIH, wIvmeH Doch veb "
"yIwIv. ghItlh yotlhDaq cursor lavIH"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Tab` / `Shift+Tab` — previous/next control"
msgstr "`Tab` / `Shift+Tab` — SeHwI' nubwI'/veb"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Home` / `End` — first/last control"
msgstr "`Home` / `End` — SeHwI' wa'DIch/Qav"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Enter` or `Space` — press the focused control"
msgstr "`Enter` pagh `Space` — SeHwI' DaSeHbogh yIyuv"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Click or tap a row that walks a list: the title steps back and the current "
"option steps forward. The `‹` and `›` on the row mark the two halves"
msgstr ""
"tetlh yItbogh tlhegh yIchu' pagh yIHot: DoH per, 'ej ghoS DaH wIvmeH Doch. "
"bID cha' luquvmoH tlheghDaq `‹` `›` je"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"The help panel is read rather than operated, so there the arrows scroll it "
"and only `Left` / `Right` move focus"
msgstr ""
"QaH 'echlet laDlu', SeHlu'be', vaj pa' 'oH vIH naQmey 'ej SeH vIH `Left` / "
"`Right` neH"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Hunting"
msgstr "wam"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Marking a player puts a cyan `◎` on their scoreboard row, a cyan ring on "
"their radar blip, and a beacon in the sky over them in their own tank colour "
"-- so several marked at once are still told apart at a glance. While one of "
"them is in your sights the HUD says **SPOTTED:** and a ping sounds once a "
"second from where they are. In Rabbit Chase the rabbit is marked for you, "
"and its beacon is cyan like its ring: everyone is hunting it, so everyone's "
"mark over it says so."
msgstr ""
"QujwI' Daghanchugh, mI' 'echlet tlheghDaq SuDqu' `◎` lan, noch Daqvetlh "
"SuDqu' ret lan, 'ej Dungvo' chalDaq wovmoHwI' lan, Dujchaj nguvmo' -- vaj "
"cha'logh law' ghanlu'chugh je, Hoch Sum ghojlaH mInlIj. DaDoStaHvIS wa' "
"**SPOTTED:** ja' HUD, 'ej Daqchajvo' wa'logh lup Hoch wab Qoylu'. Ha'DIbaH "
"wamDaq SoHvaD Ha'DIbaH ghanlu', 'ej SuDqu' wovmoHwI'Daj, retDaj rur: Hoch "
"wam 'oH, vaj 'e' maq Hoch ghanmey."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`U` — hunt: open the scoreboard cursor, and press it again on a running hunt "
"to clear every mark"
msgstr ""
"`U` — yIwam: mI' 'echlet cursor yIpoSmoH, 'ej wam QaptaHvIS Hoch ghan DateqmeH "
"yIyuvqa'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`7` — add hunt: the same cursor, but committing adds to what is marked "
"rather than replacing it, and committing on a row already marked takes it off"
msgstr ""
"`7` — wam yIchel: cursor rap, 'ach Dawuvchugh ghanlu'bogh Doch chel, choHbe'; "
"'ej tlhegh ghanlu'pu'bogh Dawuvchugh ghan teq"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Settings -> Hunt` — the same thing without a keyboard, for a phone or a "
"headset. Left and right step through `Clear` and then the players in "
"alphabetical order; select marks or unmarks whoever is shown, or clears "
"every mark on `Clear`. On a touch screen or with a mouse, tap a chevron to "
"step and anywhere else on the row to select"
msgstr ""
"`Settings -> Hunt` — Doch rap, leQ'echlet Hutlh, ghogh HablI'vaD nach "
"De'wI'vaD ghap. `Clear` vegh poS nIH je, vaj QujwI'pu' vegh, pongchaj "
"mIwvo'. 'aghlu'bogh QujwI' ghan pagh ghanHa' wIv, pagh `Clear`Daq Hoch ghan "
"teq. HotlaHbogh HaStaDaq pagh mouse lo'lu'DI', ghoSmeH tIq yIHot, 'ej "
"wIvmeH tlhegh latlh Daq yIHot"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"With the cursor open, the board's heading reads `*SEL*` and a pulsing `○` "
"sits on the row it is on, filling in to `◎` when you commit. `Up` / `Down` "
"move it, `Enter` commits, and `U` or `7` backs out keeping whatever was "
"already marked. `I` and `Space` move the cursor too, so a surface without "
"arrow keys can reach it"
msgstr ""
"cursor poSmoHlu'taHvIS, `*SEL*` ja' 'echlet per, 'ej tlheghvetlhDaq ba' "
"joqtaHbogh `○`, `◎` moj Dawuvchugh. 'oH vIH `Up` / `Down`, wuv `Enter`, "
"'ej DoH `U` pagh `7`, ghanlu'pu'bogh Doch pol. cursor vIH `I` `Space` je, "
"vaj 'oH SIchlaH naQ leQmey Hutlhbogh SeHwI'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "As an observer"
msgstr "bejwI' SoHDI'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"As an Observer you have no tank. Drive and turn fly the camera instead, "
"`Tab` climbs and `Space` descends, and holding `Shift` makes drive tilt the "
"view up and down and turn slide it sideways. The camera rests at the eye "
"height of a tank on the ground, and travel stays level however the view is "
"tilted. Pausing and self-destruct do nothing."
msgstr ""
"bejwI' SoHDI' Duj Daghajbe'. mIllogh qonwI' puv chIj tlhe' je; Dung ghoS "
"`Tab`, bIng ghoS `Space`, 'ej `Shift` Da'uchtaHvIS legh Dung bIng je "
"Sang'moH chIj, 'ej Dop ghoSmoH tlhe'. yavDaq Duj mIn 'ab ba' mIllogh qonwI', "
"'ej Sang'lu'chugh legh je, Hagh ghoSlu'taH. mevlu'chugh Qaw''eghlu'chugh "
"je, pagh qaS."

# review: the observer view names (Free, Track...) are translated, not quoted as UI strings
#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Enter` or `C` — step through everything: in each view, the leader first, "
"then every player, then on to the next view. The views are Free, Track, "
"Follow, Driving with, and Flag where a map has team flags"
msgstr ""
"`Enter` pagh `C` — Hoch Doch yIvegh: Hoch leghDaq, DevwI' wa'DIch, vaj Hoch "
"QujwI', vaj legh veb. leghmey: tlhab, ghoch, tlha', tlhej chIj, 'ej boq "
"joqwI'mey ghajchugh pu'jIn, joqwI'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`I` or right-click — in the Free view, watch the tank in your sights, or "
"show the obstacle there: what it is, an outline round it, and its block from "
"the map file with the `group` blocks that placed it"
msgstr ""
"`I` pagh nIH chu' — tlhab leghDaq, Duj DaDoSbogh yIbej, pagh pa' botwI' "
"yI'agh: nuq 'oH, Dejvo' HeH, 'ej pu'jIn ta'Daq ghItlh bIDDaj, 'oH "
"lanpu'bogh `group` bIDmey je"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Right-click or tap an obstacle anywhere on screen, in any view and the "
"Overview most of all, to show it the same way"
msgstr ""
"HaStaDaq botwI' yInIH chu' pagh yIHot, Hoch leghDaq 'ej Hoch Dung leghDaq "
"nIvqu', mIw rapDaq 'oH 'aghmeH"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Pick nothing -- the sky, or empty ground in the Overview -- or press the "
"panel's **World** button for the whole world: what is in it, faces, "
"textures, the map file's warnings and its largest meshes, each of which "
"shows that mesh"
msgstr ""
"pagh yIwIv -- chal, pagh Dung leghDaq yav chIm -- pagh qo' naQvaD 'echlet "
"**World** leQ yIyuv: Daq ngaS, qabmey, textures, pu'jIn ta' "
"ghuHmoHmey, 'ej mesh tInqu'mey; Hoch 'oH mesh'e' 'agh"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Click a scoreboard row to watch that player; click the marked row again to "
"go back to following the leader"
msgstr ""
"QujwI'vetlh DabejmeH mI' 'echlet tlhegh yIchu'; DevwI' Datlha'qa'meH, tlhegh "
"ghanlu'bogh yIchu'qa'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Mouse"
msgstr "mouse"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`M` turns mouse steering on and off, and nothing else does: the keys never "
"take it away behind your back."
msgstr ""
"mouse chIj chu' chu'Ha' je `M`, 'ej latlh Doch ta'be': not 'oH nIH leQmey "
"SoH Dalegh'be'DI'."

# review: "targeting box" coined as "DoS buq" (target bag)
#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "The targeting box"
msgstr "DoS buq"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"The two boxes in the middle of the screen are the steering, as in BZFlag. "
"Where the cursor sits relative to their centre is what the tank does:"
msgstr ""
"HaSta botlhDaq chIj 'oH buq cha''e', BZFlag rur. Duj vang ngu' cursor Daq, "
"botlhchaj DoS:"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Inside the inner box, nothing.** It is the dead zone: park the cursor "
"there to stop."
msgstr ""
"**buq qoDDaq, pagh.** Qapbe'bogh Daq 'oH: bImevmeH pa' cursor yIlan."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Between the boxes, more the further out.** Up is forward and down is "
"reverse; left and right turn. Each grows evenly from nothing at the inner "
"box's edge to full at the outer box's."
msgstr ""
"**buqmey ngeDDaq, Hop DaghoSchugh, law'.** ghoS Dung, DoH bIng; tlhe' poS "
"nIH je. qoD buq HeHDaq pagh, Hur buq HeHDaq naQ; Hoch ghur ghoD."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**At or past the outer box, full.** Each axis stops growing on its own, so "
"running the cursor out past the top keeps the tank at full speed and leaves "
"left and right free to steer."
msgstr ""
"**Hur buqDaq pagh juSDI', naQ.** nIteb ghurbe'choH Hoch tlhegh, vaj Dung "
"HeH Dajuschugh cursor, Do naQ ghajtaH Duj, 'ej poS nIH je chIjmeH tlhab."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Reverse is half speed**, as it is from the keys, however far down the "
"cursor goes."
msgstr ""
"**Do bID ghaj DoH**, leQmey rur, bIng Hop ghoSchugh cursor je."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**The box sets the speed asked for, not the speed you get at once.** A world "
"with an acceleration limit (BZFlag's `-a`, off by default) brings the tank "
"up to it over time, the same as it does from the keys."
msgstr ""
"**Do poQlu'bogh lan buq; Do DaSuqbogh nom lanbe'.** Do ghurmeH veH ghajchugh "
"qo' (BZFlag `-a`, motlh Qapbe'), ruchmo' poH Do Suq Duj, leQmey rur."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"The boxes are BZFlag's own sizes, scaled to the window. BZFlag also holds "
"the cursor inside the box; a browser cannot without taking the pointer over, "
"so in bzo the cursor can leave it -- the steering simply stays at full, and "
"the cost is a longer move back to the centre."
msgstr ""
"BZFlag buqmey Hugh rap ghaj buqmey, Qorwagh lughoD. buq qoDDaq cursor "
"'uch BZFlag je; cursor yonbe'chugh, ta'laHbe' De' nejwI', vaj bzoDaq "
"buq mejlaH cursor -- naQtaH chIj, 'ej botlhDaq chegh nI'qu' 'oH DIl'e'."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"With the keys, the mouse keeps whichever axis no key is holding -- see "
"[Combining inputs](#combining-inputs)."
msgstr ""
"leQmey lo'lu'DI', nIteb tlhegh 'uchbe'bogh leQ pol mouse -- yIlegh [SeHmey "
"muv](#combining-inputs)."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Clicks"
msgstr "chu'mey"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Left click shoots wherever the cursor is, whether mouse steering is on or "
"not, unless the click lands on the chat panel or a button. Right click "
"identifies. Mouse steering is unavailable with no mouse attached, in VR, and "
"while the on-screen controls are up, since those steer instead; a click that "
"misses one of their buttons does nothing rather than firing."
msgstr ""
"poS chu' bach cursor Daqvo', mouse chIj chu'lu'chugh chu'lu'be'chugh je, "
"ja'chuq 'echletDaq leQDaq ghap chu'be'chugh. ngu' nIH chu'. mouse "
"rarlu'be'chugh, qo' ngebDaq, HaSta SeHmey 'aghlu'taHvIS je, mouse chIj "
"Dalo'laHbe', chIjmo' SeHmeyvetlh; leQchaj ngoQbe'bogh chu' bachbe', pagh "
"qaS."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Combining inputs"
msgstr "SeHmey muv"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Every input drives at once, and nothing switches between them on its own: "
"`M` and the Settings rows are the only things that change which ones are on."
msgstr ""
"rap poHDaq chIj Hoch SeHwI', 'ej nIteb choHbe' vay': chu'lu'bogh SeHwI'mey "
"choH `M` SeHlaw tlheghmey je neH."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Driving is shared out an axis at a time** -- forward/back, and turn, each "
"on its own. On each, the first of these with something to say wins:"
msgstr ""
"**wa' tlhegh wa' poH, chIj ngoplu'** -- ghoS/DoH, tlhe' je, nIteb Hoch. "
"Hoch tlheghDaq, Qap Dochmeyvam wa'DIch, ja'meH Doch ghajbogh:"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Keys.** A held drive key owns its axis, and holding both of a pair (`W` "
"and `S`, or `A` and `D`) is a deliberate stop on that axis."
msgstr ""
"**leQmey.** tlheghDaj ghaj chIj leQ 'uchlu'bogh, 'ej cha' leQ Da'uchchugh "
"(`W` `S` je, pagh `A` `D` je), tlheghvetlhDaq bImev 'e' DaNIDbogh."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**The stick:** the XR controllers in VR, otherwise a connected gamepad, "
"otherwise the on-screen stick. Only one of the three is read at a time -- "
"they are not added together."
msgstr ""
"**naQ:** qo' ngebDaq XR SeHwI'mey, pagh rarlu'bogh Quj SeHwI', pagh HaSta "
"naQ. rap poHDaq wej Doch wa' neH laDlu' -- boqHa'lu'be'."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "**The mouse**, in the targeting box, with mouse steering on."
msgstr "**mouse**, DoS buqDaq, mouse chIj chu'lu'DI'."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"So you can drive with `W` while the mouse steers, turn with `A`/`D` while "
"the mouse sets the speed, or steer a gamepad's turn while a key holds the "
"speed. A stick let go reads zero and gives the axis to the mouse; the mouse "
"box holds whatever the cursor's place says, which is why it comes last."
msgstr ""
"vaj chIjtaHvIS mouse, `W` lo'taHvIS bIghoSlaH; Do lantaHvIS mouse, `A`/`D` "
"lo'taHvIS bItlhe'laH; pagh Do 'uchtaHvIS leQ, Quj SeHwI' tlhe' DachIjlaH. "
"naQ Dachaghchugh, pagh laD 'ej mouse nob tlhegh; cursor Daq ja'bogh Doch "
"'uch mouse buq, vaj Qav ghoS."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Buttons add up.** Shoot fires from `Enter`, a left click, or the stick "
"source's own fire button; jump from `Tab` or the stick source's; identify "
"from `I`, a right click, or the stick source's. Any of them will do."
msgstr ""
"**leQmey boqlu'.** `Enter`, poS chu', naQ bachmeH leQ ghap lo'lu'chugh "
"bachlu'; `Tab` naQ leQ ghap lo'lu'chugh Suplu'; `I`, nIH chu', naQ leQ "
"ghap lo'lu'chugh ngu'lu'. Hoch Qap."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**With the autopilot on**, the pilot takes the mouse's place, last in line: "
"a drive key or the stick you hold still owns its axis, and the pilot has the "
"rest. So when it is wedged against something you can hold `A` to turn it "
"out, or `S` to back it off, while it keeps the other axis, and let go to "
"hand it back -- it carries on from wherever you left it, re-planning its "
"route if you took it somewhere else. Your shots, jumps and drops add to its "
"own. The mouse box does not steer while the autopilot drives: it holds an "
"offset wherever the cursor is parked, so it would never hand anything back."
msgstr ""
"**nIteb chIjwI' chu'lu'DI'**, mouse Daq tlhap chIjwI', Qav: chIj leQ naQ "
"ghap Da'uchbogh tlheghDaj ghajtaH, 'ej latlh ghaj chIjwI'. vaj vay'Daq "
"rarchoHchugh, ghaH Datlhe'moHmeH `A` Da'uchlaH, pagh ghaH DaDoHmoHmeH `S`, "
"latlh tlhegh poltaHvIS ghaH, 'ej ghaHvaD Danobqa'meH yIchagh -- Daq "
"Damejbogh ghaHvo' ghoStaH, 'ej latlh Daq DaQengchugh He nablaHqa'. "
"bachmeylIj, Supmey, chaghmey je ghaH Dochmey chel. nIteb chIjwI' chIjtaHvIS "
"chIjbe' mouse buq: cursor Daqvo' Hop Do 'uch, vaj not vay' nobqa'."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Menus don't stop the autopilot.** Opening Settings, or any other menu, "
"normally pauses your tank. With the autopilot driving, the menu takes the "
"keys and the pilot goes on driving. With a pilot chosen on the `Settings -> "
"Autopilot` row but not driving, opening a menu turns the autopilot on, and "
"closing the menu turns it off again -- so a menu means \"drive for me a "
"moment\" rather than \"stop\". With the row on `None`, the default, or on a "
"server that refuses bots (`-disableBots`), menus pause as they always have. "
"A hidden window still pauses either way: the browser stops drawing it, and "
"the pilot with it."
msgstr ""
"**nIteb chIjwI' mevmoHbe' HIDjolevmey.** SeHlaw pagh latlh HIDjolev "
"DapoSmoHchugh, motlh DujlIj mevmoH. chIjtaH nIteb chIjwI'chugh, leQmey "
"tlhap HIDjolev 'ej chIjtaH chIjwI'. `Settings -> Autopilot` tlheghDaq "
"chIjwI' wIvlu'pu'chugh 'ach chIjbe'chugh, HIDjolev DapoSmoHchugh nIteb "
"chIjwI' chu'lu', 'ej HIDjolev DaSoQmoHchugh chu'Ha'lu'qa' -- vaj \"qen "
"jIHvaD yIchIj\" 'oH HIDjolev, \"yImev\" 'oHbe'. `None` (motlh) Daq "
"tlhegh, pagh De'wI' QujwI'pu' lajQo'bogh toy' De'wI' (`-disableBots`), "
"reH HIDjolevmey mevmoH. Qorwagh So'lu'bogh mevmoH reH: 'oH nargh 'e' mev "
"De' nejwI', 'ej chIjwI' je."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Three keys at once.** Many keyboards cannot report some three-key "
"combinations at all -- the third key's press never reaches the browser -- so "
"a held turn and reverse can swallow a jump (#146). The debug HUD (`` ` ``) "
"shows how many keys the browser saw held at once, which tells the keyboard's "
"limit from bzo's."
msgstr ""
"**rap poHDaq wej leQmey.** wej leQ muvmey 'op ja'laHbe' leQ'echletmey law' "
"-- not De' nejwI' SIch wejDIch leQ yuvlu'bogh -- vaj Sup ghup tlhe' DoH je "
"'uchlu'bogh (#146). rap poHDaq leQmey 'uchlu'bogh 'ar legh De' nejwI' 'e' "
"'agh Qagh HUD (`` ` ``), vaj leQ'echlet veH bzo veH je Sum ghojlaH."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Touch: the on-screen controls"
msgstr "Hot: HaSta SeHmey"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"A phone starts with them on; anywhere else `Settings -> Virtual Controls` "
"turns them on and off."
msgstr ""
"ghogh HablI'Daq chu'lu'taH tagh; latlh DaqDaq, chu' chu'Ha' je `Settings -> "
"Virtual Controls`."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**The stick**, bottom left: push it to drive and turn, as far as you push "
"it. A mouse can drag it too."
msgstr ""
"**naQ**, bIng poS: bIchIjmeH bItlhe'meH je yIyuv; Hop Dayuvchugh, law'. "
"'oH lISlaH mouse je."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**`●`** — shoot. Tapping fires as fast as clicking a mouse; holding fires at "
"the world's sustained rate"
msgstr ""
"**`●`** — yIbach. DaHotchugh, mouse chu' rur nom bach; Da'uchchugh, qo' Do "
"motlh bach"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "**`⤒`** — jump"
msgstr "**`⤒`** — yISup"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "**`⚑`** — drop flag"
msgstr "**`⚑`** — joqwI' yIchagh"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "**`◎`** — identify, and lock a Guided Missile"
msgstr "**`◎`** — yIngu', 'ej peng SeHlu'bogh yIDoSmoH"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Everything else -- camera, radar range, chat, hunting, autopilot, pausing -- "
"is a row in Settings, which a tap reaches."
msgstr ""
"latlh Hoch -- mIllogh qonwI', noch chuq, ja'chuq, wam, nIteb chIjwI', mev -- "
"SeHlaw tlhegh 'oH, 'ej Hotlu'chugh SIchlu'."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Gamepad"
msgstr "Quj SeHwI'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Any controller the browser reports in the standard layout (most USB and "
"Bluetooth pads, and iOS MFi controllers). Plugging one in turns it on; "
"nothing needs setting up."
msgstr ""
"motlh mIwDaq SeHwI' ja'bogh De' nejwI' Hoch (USB Bluetooth je SeHwI'mey "
"law'qu', iOS MFi SeHwI'mey je). wa' Dararchugh chu'lu'; pagh lanlu'nIS."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Control"
msgstr "SeHwI'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "In a menu"
msgstr "HIDjolevDaq"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Left stick"
msgstr "poS naQ"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "forward/backward and turn"
msgstr "ghoS/DoH 'ej tlhe'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "move between rows, change a row"
msgstr "tlheghmey ngeDDaq yIvIH, tlhegh yIchoH"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`A` / Cross, or right trigger"
msgstr "`A` / Cross, pagh nIH chu'wI'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "shoot"
msgstr "yIbach"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "select"
msgstr "yIwIv"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`B` / Circle, or left trigger"
msgstr "`B` / Circle, pagh poS chu'wI'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "jump"
msgstr "yISup"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "back"
msgstr "yIchegh"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`X` / Square"
msgstr "`X` / Square"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "drop flag"
msgstr "joqwI' yIchagh"

# review: "shoulder button" rendered as one shoulder (volchaH)
#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Either shoulder"
msgstr "wa' volchaH"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "identify"
msgstr "yIngu'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"The sticks have a dead zone of a fifth of their travel, so a pad left on the "
"desk does not creep. The right stick is free."
msgstr ""
"naQmey vIHmeH chuq cha'maH vatlhvI' Qapbe'bogh Daq 'oH, vaj raSDaq SeHwI' "
"lanlu'chugh vIHbe'. tlhab nIH naQ."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"The pad rumbles when you fire and when your tank dies, as BZFlag's does: a "
"short buzz for a shot, longer for a shock wave, both motors for a laser, and "
"one long, strong shake for a death. It rumbles only while it is what you are "
"playing with -- a key or a click hands control back and keeps it quiet -- "
"and never for an observer. **Rumble** in Settings turns it off. The browser "
"has to support it; Chrome and Edge do."
msgstr ""
"bIbachDI' Hegh DujlIj je Qom SeHwI', BZFlag rur: nIchvaD Qom ngaj, "
"jorwI'vaD Qom nI', tIHvaD cha' QuQ, 'ej HeghvaD wa' Qom nI' HoS. "
"DaQujmeH Dalo'taHvIS neH Qom -- SeH chegh leQ chu' ghap, 'ej tam -- 'ej "
"not bejwI'vaD Qom. 'oH chu'Ha' SeHlaw **Rumble**. 'oH QaHnIS De' nejwI'; "
"QaH Chrome Edge je."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "XR controllers"
msgstr "XR SeHwI'mey"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"In VR the controllers are the only input. Turning the tank is independent of "
"where you look."
msgstr ""
"qo' ngebDaq SeHwI'mey neH lo'lu'. Daq Dabejbogh lumbe' Duj tlhe'."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "In the XR menu"
msgstr "XR HIDjolevDaq"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Either thumbstick"
msgstr "wa' naQ"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "forward/backward and turn -- the right stick if both are pushed"
msgstr "ghoS/DoH 'ej tlhe' -- cha' yuvlu'chugh, nIH naQ Qap"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Either trigger"
msgstr "wa' chu'wI'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`A` / `X` (primary face button)"
msgstr "`A` / `X` (wa'DIch leQ)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`B` / `Y` (secondary face button)"
msgstr "`B` / `Y` (cha'DIch leQ)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "open the XR menu"
msgstr "XR HIDjolev yIpoSmoH"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "back, and close it from the top"
msgstr "yIchegh, 'ej Dungvo' yISoQmoH"

# review: "grip" rendered as "ghop 'uchwI'" (hand holder)
#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Either grip"
msgstr "wa' ghop 'uchwI'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Press either thumbstick"
msgstr "wa' naQ yIyuv"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Both controllers pulse for the same events as a gamepad's rumble."
msgstr "Quj SeHwI' Qom rur, wanI' rapvaD Qom cha' SeHwI'."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Identify is on the thumbstick press because a thumb that is steering presses "
"it by accident, and identifying costs nothing; the menu is on `B` for the "
"same reason. Typing -- a name, a MOTD -- uses the headset's own system "
"keyboard, raised when the row takes focus; see the README's WebXR section "
"for headsets that have none."
msgstr ""
"naQ yuvlu'DI' ngu'lu', chIjtaHbogh nItlh SIS 'oH yuvmo' 'ej pagh DIl ngu'; "
"meq rapmo' `B`Daq HIDjolev tu'lu'. ghItlhDI' -- pong, MOTD ghap -- nach "
"De'wI' leQ'echlet lo'lu', tlhegh SeHlu'DI' 'aghlu'; leQ'echlet Hutlhbogh "
"nach De'wI'mey DaghojmeH, README WebXR 'ay' yIlaD."

#: docs/help/flags.md
msgid "Flags"
msgstr "joqwI'mey"

#: docs/help/flags.md
msgid ""
"Drive over a flag to pick it up, and `Space` to drop it. Good flags help; "
"bad flags hinder, and stay until they shake off, you kill, or you die. A "
"superflag on the ground is white and tells you nothing about itself until "
"somebody picks it up. Team flags are captured by carrying an enemy's to your "
"own base."
msgstr ""
"joqwI' DatlhapmeH 'oH Dung yIchIj, 'ej 'oH DachaghmeH `Space` yIlo'. QaH "
"joqwI'mey QaQ; botlh joqwI'mey qab, 'ej ratlh, chaghchoHpa', bIHoHpa', "
"bIHeghpa' ghap. yavDaq joqwI' nIv chIS 'oH, 'ej vay' tlhappa' 'oH, SoHvaD "
"pagh ja'. jagh boq joqwI' DatlhapmeH, juHlIjDaq yIqeng."

#: docs/help/scoreboard.md
msgid "Scoreboard"
msgstr "mI' 'echlet"

#: docs/help/scoreboard.md
msgid ""
"Each row's numbers read **Kills / Deaths**, then **[Team Kills]** once you "
"have any, then your own record against that one opponent: **wins~losses**, "
"blank until you've actually fought them. Your own row shows a self-destruct "
"count there instead, since you have no record against yourself. Rabbit Chase "
"adds a rank percentage in front of the kill count."
msgstr ""
"Hoch tlhegh mI'mey: **HoH / Hegh**, vaj **[boq HoH]**, wa' DaghajDI', vaj "
"jaghvetlh DaSuvmeH qun: **Qapla'~luj**, chIm, ghaH DaSuvpa'. tlheghlIjDaq "
"Qaw''egh mI' 'aghlu', bI'eghvaD qun Daghajbe'mo'. HoH mI' tlhopDaq patlh "
"vatlhvI' chel Ha'DIbaH wam."

#: docs/help/scoreboard.md
msgid ""
"Before a name, in cyan: `@` means that player is an admin, `+` means they're "
"signed in with a verified callsign this session. Neither shows for anyone "
"else."
msgstr ""
"pong tlhopDaq, SuDqu': loHwI' 'oH QujwI'vetlh 'e' maq `@`; DaH pong "
"'ollu'pu'bogh lo'taHvIS 'el ghaH 'e' maq `+`. latlhvaD Dochvam 'aghlu'be'."

#: docs/help/scoreboard.md
msgid ""
"Right after the name itself: a `/XX` is the flag they're carrying, in that "
"flag's own colour -- see [Flags](flags.md) for what each abbreviation means."
msgstr ""
"pong ret: ghaH joqwI' qengbogh 'oH `/XX`'e', joqwI'vetlh nguvDaq -- Hoch "
"pong ngaj QIjmeH yIlegh [joqwI'mey](flags.md)."

#: docs/help/scoreboard.md
msgid ""
"Further along the name: 🎤 means that player's microphone is on, and 🔊 "
"replaces it the moment they're actually speaking. ⏳ means paused. A hunted "
"player wears a cyan `◎` -- see [Hunting](controls.md#hunting)."
msgstr ""
"pong veb: QujwI'vetlh ghogh jan chu'lu' 'e' maq 🎤, 'ej jatlhDI' ghaH 'oH "
"tam 🔊. mevlu' 'e' maq ⏳. QujwI' wamlu'bogh SuDqu' `◎` tuQ -- yIlegh "
"[wam](controls.md#hunting)."

#: docs/help/voice.md
msgid "Audio and voice"
msgstr "wab ghogh je"

#: docs/help/voice.md
msgid ""
"`Settings -> Audio Settings` — game, voice, and microphone levels, each from "
"Off to 100%"
msgstr ""
"`Settings -> Audio Settings` — Quj, ghogh, ghogh jan je HoS, Hoch "
"chu'Ha'lu'bogh vo' 100% ghoS"

#: docs/help/voice.md
msgid ""
"**Voice channel** — **All** is everyone on the server, **Nearby** is only "
"players within earshot, **Team** is your own team anywhere on the map"
msgstr ""
"**ghogh He** — toy' De'wI'Daq Hoch 'oH **Hoch**'e', QujwI'pu' Qoylu'laHbogh "
"neH 'oH **Sumbogh**'e', pu'jInDaq Daq Hoch boqlIj 'oH **boq**'e'"

#: docs/help/voice.md
msgid "`B` — toggle the microphone"
msgstr "`B` — ghogh jan yIchu'/yIchu'Ha'"

#: docs/help/voice.md
msgid ""
"Voice is available after microphone permission is granted. Observers talk "
"and listen on the same terms as everyone else."
msgstr ""
"ghogh jan lo'meH chaw' nobpu'DI', ghogh lo'laH. latlh rur jatlh 'ej 'Ijlu' "
"bejwI'pu'."

